{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/322188-hack-whimsy-alternate-seeming-blessings-and-curses","id":322188,"title":"[Hack?Whimsy] Alternate Seeming Blessings and Curses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-25T14:20:44-08:00","id":322188,"title":"[Hack?Whimsy] Alternate Seeming Blessings and Curses","content":"So, I got bored... and I apparently decided to write this. Don't ask me why! <hr /> <b>Sidebar: Touch of Glamour</b><br /> Every Changeling is capable of drawing on their Mien, pulling a touch of Glamour into this world.<br /> As a Reflexive action, a Changeling may spend 1 Glamour to enhance one of their Traits for a Scene; the Traits they may enhance are determined by their Seeming.<br /> Any dice pool (other than Contract activation) involving the enhanced trait gains a bonus equal to the Changeling's Wyrd; this bonus does not stack with itself. If an enhanced Trait is used as a Resistance Trait, it receives a bonus equal to one-half of the Changeling's Wyrd, rounded up. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Beasts</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Touch of Glamour:</b> Beasts may use the Touch of Glamour to enhance Athletics, Composure, and Survival.<br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Any action a Beast makes that makes that symbolically represents the animal they were (and are) receives a +2 bonus.<br /> <b>Curse:</b> Beasts carry a wildness in their breast and eye, an instinctive rejection of intellect; for a Beast, the Untrained penalty for mental skills is -4, and they also lose the 10-again quality on Intelligence rolls.</div><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Darklings</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Touch of Glamour:</b> Darklings may use the Touch of Glamour to enhance Stealth, Subterfuge, and Wits.<br /> <b>Blessing:</b> While a Darkling is in darkness or in shadows, any roll they make that takes advantage of that fact receives a +2 bonus.<br /> <b>Curse:</b> A Darkling's magic is the magic of the night, and of dark, secret places; as such, they take a -1 penalty on all Contract activation rolls during the day. In addition, they lose the 10-again quality on Contract activation rolls while they are in direct sunlight.</div><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Elementals</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Touch of Glamour:</b> Elementals may use the Touch of Glamour to enhance Stamina and Resolve.<br /> <b>Blessing:</b> An Elemental receives a +2 bonus on any roll that directly concerns their element.<br /> <b>Curse:</b> There is something inhuman flitting behind an Elemental's eye; they cannot help but be somewhat alien. Elementals take a -1 penalty to all rolls predicated on the ability to predict the actions and responses of others; in addition, they lose the 10-again quality on all Manipulation rolls.</div><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Fairest</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Touch of Glamour:</b> Fairest may use the Touch of Glamour to enhance Persuasion, Presence, and Socialize.<br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Fairest gains a +2 bonus on any actions they take while 'in the spotlight'.<br /> <b>Curse:</b> The Fairest are the closest to the Kindly Ones that took them away (as much as they hate to admit it). As such, Fairest take a -1 penalty to all Breaking Point rolls. Additionally, they lose the 10-again quality on Breaking Point rolls caused by isolation from mundane humans or by contact with Arcadia and its Gentry.</div><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ogres</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Touch of Glamour:</b> Ogres may use the Touch of Glamour to enhance Brawl, Intimidate, and Strength.<br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Ogres receive a +2 bonus on any roll that employs brute force, whether physical, mental, or social.<br /> <b>Curse:</b> An Ogre's ability to hold their temper and reign in their urges was compromised while they were in Arcadia; as such, their Composure is reduced by 1 for the purposes of using it as a Resistance Trait. In addition, they lose the 10-again quality on any non-Perception Composure rolls.</div><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Wizened</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Touch of Glamour:</b> Wizened may use the Touch of Glamour to enhance Dexterity and Intelligence.<br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Wizened gain a +2 bonus on all actions that are ritualistic or extensively pre-planned.<br /> <b>Curse:</b> The Wizened were left socially small and short-tempered; they take a -2 penalty when using social skills untrained. In addition, they lose the 10-Again quality on all Presence rolls.</div><hr /><br /> If anyone's interested, I can probably hack together a translation of the Kiths too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-17-2014, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T17:09:52-08:00","id":322269,"title":"","content":"<b>Blessing:</b> A Fairest inverts the untrained penalty for social skills; instead of taking a -1 penalty, they receive a +1 bonus to all uses of Untrained social skills.<br /> <br /> Might want to adjust this a little, essentially right now it rewards not putting ranks in social skills. I feel that a blessing should reward you for playing to type, rather than rewarding you for playing against type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T18:28:55-08:00","id":322299,"title":"","content":"My argument is that it actually <i>does</i> reward you for playing to type.<br /> <br /> Normally, you have to drop at least some points in Persuasion, Empathy, Socialize, and Subterfuge to be generally competent as a social character.<br /> <br /> Fairest... don't. They have a &quot;natural&quot; aptitude towards being social; even if they are social Tertiary, Fairest can give a decent showing as a social character.<br /> <br /> If that makes any sense.<br /> <hr /><br /> After some thought, I changed Touch of Glamour's progression so that it's smoother.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:00:57-08:00","id":322336,"title":"","content":"The thing is, this blessing goes away when you put dots in skills, meaning the skills the player is interested in using and developing will be the ones unaffected by their blessing, if that makes sense. Basically, if I'm playing Fairest who's an artist, I'll naturally want to focus on expression, and probably empathy -- so the things I care about aren't going to be influenced at all by my being a Fairest (unless it's a Presence roll, and I choose to spend glamour to pump it up), while things I don't care about, like, say, Intimidation will be. It's just sort of counter-intuitive. With this system, even a Fairest who's got a dot in subterfuge is on equal footing with a Fairest who has no dots in subterfuge, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:14:02-08:00","id":322339,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting schema you've cooked up. I'll have to take a closer look when I have more time, but I like it overall, at first blush. ^_^ Though I do share raygungoth and Murder-Chan's concern.<br /> <br /> I certainly dig the idea that Fairest have a certain natural \u00e9lan, but, well... If someone's playing a Fairest, there's a very high chance that character's meant to excel in at least one social area, which means they're not likely to stop at untrained. As Murder-chan notes, a Fairest who starts with one or more dots in all social skills gets nothing at all from this blessing. If a Fairest goes from 0 to 1 dot in-play, that's experience spent for gaining only the ability to purchase the second dot; I mean, yeah, the Fairest already started with that benefit, but there's a reason nobody likes dead levels in D&amp;D. In addition, Touch of Glamour already leaves even an untrained Fairest pretty well served in the social arena, so the innate social aptitude angle is sort of covered.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would be worth considering a tweak so that all Fairest derive some benefit, whether or not they've invested in social skills. I'm away from my books and haven't touched things in ages (I couldn't recite all mental skills with a gun to my head), but it may be worth giving the Wizened blessing a second look for similar reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:14:03-08:00","id":322340,"title":"","content":"True...<br /> <br /> I'll think of something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:28:50-08:00","id":322349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/322188-hack-whimsy-alternate-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=322336#post322336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, this blessing goes away when you put dots in skills, meaning the skills the player is interested in using and developing will be the ones unaffected by their blessing, if that makes sense. Basically, if I'm playing Fairest who's an artist, I'll naturally want to focus on expression, and probably empathy -- so the things I care about aren't going to be influenced at all by my being a Fairest (unless it's a Presence roll, and I choose to spend glamour to pump it up), while things I don't care about, like, say, Intimidation will be. It's just sort of counter-intuitive. With this system, even a Fairest who's got a dot in subterfuge is on equal footing with a Fairest who has no dots in subterfuge, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> It doesn't reward you for playing type, you have to spend 4 XP <i>per skill</i> to play at type. That's a little rough - if you ask me, I'd suggest figuring out either a +2 they can get somewhere (and do that to Wizened, as well) or make Blessings be a little cooler than a +1/+2 or something. Like, if you want them to have a natural social aptitude, try something like allowing them to have one tier of leverage up on the chart, or increase an impression by one or lower it or whatever, or the ability to automatically ignore a certain amount of doors, or something even really out there like learning the lowest of someone's Social traits or the lowest of Power, Finesse, or Resistance.<br /> <br /> For Wizened, ugh. Now it feels like being punished just for playing the game. However, I feel like current Wizened do that already (unless you're trying to make a back-flipping battle butler, then they're insane), so that's not too far off the mark. I've always thought the Wizened blessing should reflect that Seeming better. They're &quot;little people&quot; and &quot;wise women&quot; and alien abductors who perform outrageous experiments. If there's a rule they have to follow, they ought to know it, even if they don't know what it means. One possibility is allowing them to all have the right tool at the right time - like a souped-up Shiv merit. You don't take a penalty for not having a tool.<br /> <br /> I really like <b>Touch of Glamour</b>, I am incorporating it into my dieselpunk setting for all clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:45:58-08:00","id":322370,"title":"","content":"The basic idea was for Seemings to be on an even footing - they get Touch of Glamour for either 2 Attributes or an Attribute and 2 Skills, they get a +2 bonus in a wide niche, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Then, Kiths are where you get your interesting little powers. I mean, the Seemings have to be pretty generic, after all.<br /> <br /> Following with that...<br /> <br /> As long as one of the <b>Fairest</b> is poised, they receive a +2 bonus on any roll that takes advantage of that fact.<br /> The <b>Wizened</b> gain a +2 bonus on any roll involving ritual or precision. <hr />I'm not as happy with the Fairest one; the idea is to encourage them to act like they're in control <i>all the time</i>.<br /> <br /> Almost like cats, in a way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T20:03:20-08:00","id":322372,"title":"","content":"Actually, that's pretty awesome. I'm just not a huge fan of bonuses and penalties in general - I prefer those to be situational, and then have abilities that add options, rather than mainlining with brute force (also, the only Seemings that ever seemed broad and generic to me are Wizened and Elementals).<br /> <br /> Hm. What about whenever the Fairest is making a roll involving convincing someone of something - truth or not? That way they can get the bonus for intimidating or sweet-talking or seeming like they're cool when they're not cool, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T20:21:42-08:00","id":322380,"title":"","content":"That might work...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T22:00:31-08:00","id":322408,"title":"","content":"wouldn't that be all Social rolls? Seems really broad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T23:31:30-08:00","id":322460,"title":"","content":"Hmm... As long as you're coming up with alternative Blessings here, have you considered revising the one Beasts get? I can see a wide range of contexts in which members of the other Seemings might use (or be tempted to use) their Blessing,* and the Beast's looks really one-note by comparison. I mean, I agree an appropriate specialty and bonuses in Animal Ken are logical, just as they are in the canon version, but they've also never been very interesting or exciting to me. Maybe I'm alone in that. Its usefulness felt like it varied too wildly (eheh...) with the animal in question: it can range from actually coming up reasonably often and being potentially handy to cropping up essentially never and being pretty worthless even when it does. I've honestly always thought the option to buff Presence and Composure pools was the <i>real</i> Blessing, with the Animal Ken bonuses as a flavorful side-note. If anyone's actual play experience has been different, I have little myself, so I'd be very pleased to hear about it.<br /> <br /> If you'd consider changing it, I can understand the difficulty in what should replace it. I did like the idea of the Blessing involving or depending on the character's particular animal. I'd be very fond of some kind of bonus/benefit to the character when acting in a manner that especially resonates with or draws on the animal's nature, or at least an anthropomorphized nature ascribed to it. Said nature may need spelling out and narrowing, to avoid it becoming pretty much a bonus to every action for some creatures. Could also potentially cover all sorts of interactions with or knowledge of that sort of animal. Maybe both together with a +1...? Just takin' shots in the dark, here.<br /> <br /> * I like that Ogres are at their strongest when they're applying brute force of all stripes. Even a relatively meek Ogre who'd prefer not to be forceful has to deal with knowing that it's never really a terrible option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tweaking suggestion wording. 11-26-2014, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T05:46:03-08:00","id":322741,"title":"","content":"Would not the best for Fairest to just give them 8-again on Social rolls? That way, if you at least have 1 dice left, they can get pretty good rolls. And that with they having dicepools of about 10 come to awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T09:41:55-08:00","id":322887,"title":"","content":"I understand the reasoning regarding Beast\u00b4s blessing, but I still think Animal Ken is usually the less useful skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T14:10:30-08:00","id":336280,"title":"","content":"I updated the <b>Beast</b>, <b>Fairest</b>, and <b>Wizened</b> to be more in line with the others.<br /> <br /> Now the Beast gives you an incentive to be feral, the Fairest are <i>always</i> better when they're the center of attention, and Wizened work best when they've got a plan to work from.<br /> <br /> Would anyone like to see <b>Kiths</b>, <b>Mantles</b>, or <b>Seeming Evolutions</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T18:27:14-08:00","id":336555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/322188-hack-whimsy-alternate-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=336280#post336280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anyone like to see <b>Kiths</b>, <b>Mantles</b>, or <b>Seeming Evolutions</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Me, me, me! This Hack is great! I wanna see all three. Could you please make the three for Mechanicals too, if you have the time?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T20:04:57-08:00","id":336655,"title":"","content":"The nice thing about doing everything by a formula is that it's pretty easy to throw together new stuff for seemings. I haven't really figured out what I'm doing with Kiths yet, so the Mantles are probably going to be first.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, strike that... my idea for Mantles requires me to finish up Kiths first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-11-2014, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T00:22:24-08:00","id":336814,"title":"","content":"Just as a teaser, here are most of the Darklings:<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Sidebar - Harvesting Glamour from Emotions:</b> A Changeling may attempt to harvest Glamour from another character's emotions. They may not harvest from the Gentry, the denizens of Arcadia or the Hedge, or from other Changelings (a bitter reminder of their inhuman state). They may only draw Glamour from a given character once per scene, and each Changeling who has done so earlier that scene imposes a cumulative -1 penalty on the roll to harvest.<br /> <br /> Harvesting Glamour requires that the Changeling make a roll appropriate to their methods; an Ogre might use Strength + Intimidate when attempting to draw strength from fear, while a Spring courtier might use Presence + Persuasion to... coax some Glamour out of someone. A Changeling may harvest Glamour in combat - doing so is an Instant action, and therefore takes up their turn.<br /> <br /> A Success on a harvesting roll gives the Changeling 1 Glamour; an Exceptional Success gives them 3 Glamour. If the emotion is especially sharp, intense, or consuming, the Changeling gains an additional point of Glamour. Conversely, attempting to draw Glamour from an especially weak or transient emotion applies a penalty from -1 to -3, and any Failures are automatically Dramatic Failures.<br /> <br /> Each Changeling Court has an emotion associated to it; whenever a courtier harvests Glamour from their Court's emotion, they gain an additional point of Glamour.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>Antiquarians:</b> Keepers of dark lore in darker libraries, Antiquarians benefit from <i>Archivist's Diligence</i>; they gain a +3 bonus to all Research rolls made in light no brighter than a candle.<br /> <br /> <b>Gravewights:</b> Blessed (or cursed) with the ability to interact with spectres, Gravewights possess the <i>Medium's Gift</i>; they may hear, see, and speak to Ghosts in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <b>Leechfinger:</b> In Arcadia, they were the hunger hidden by the dark; even after their return, they retain the <i>Hunger for Life</i>. Whenever they successfully harvest Glamour from an emotion in a way that involves physical contact, they may choose to deal 1L to their victim. If they do so, they reduce the amount of Glamour they gain by 1 and heal 1 HL of Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Lurker:</b> Back in Faerie, they hid in the shadows and fled from the unblinking eyes of their captors; they still can <i>Flee like Shadows</i>, imposing a -2 penalty on all attempts to perceive them while they're in the dark.<br /> <br /> <b>Mirrorskin:</b> Mirrorskin were shadowy spies or infiltrators during their Durance; they still have <i>Flesh like Clay</i>, allowing them to mold their appearance. This grants them a +3 bonus on any Wits + Subterfuge rolls they make to disguise themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightsinger:</b> Nightsingers serenaded and cajolled in the dark; with their <i>Nightingale's Voice</i>, they could sing with preternatural strength and clarity. Whenever the Nightsinger sings in the dark, their voice carries twice as far, and they gain a +2 bonus on the Expression roll if the song is intended to provoke an emotion or entice the listener.<br /> <br /> <b>Razorhands:</b> Razorhands were used as murderers and assassins amongst the Gentry (though those deaths never stuck) - they still have their <i>Faithful Demodands</i>. As such, a Razorhand may pull a mundane Knife out of the shadows as a Reflexive action; if the knife is separated from them somehow, it returns to the darkness the first chance it gets.<br /> <br /> <b>Tunnelgrub:</b> Some unlucky Changelings were buried in the dark and forced to find their way; they can still <i>Wriggle and Writhe</i>, allowing them to act as if they were 2 sizes smaller for the purposes of fitting into tight spaces.<br /> <hr /><br /> I have most of the Beasts covered, as well as the above Darklings, and a few of the Elementals. My basic philosophy is to hand out a passive benefit, because your Kith is what you <i>are</i>, not some power you're drawing on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T02:32:42-08:00","id":339880,"title":"","content":"In the Beast case, what can be interpreted as &quot;feral&quot;? one must remember their seeming reflects the &quot;literary&quot;concept associated to animals rather than the real deal. Example: regal lions, cowardly hyenas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 12-14-2014, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:26:30-08:00","id":340190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/322188-hack-whimsy-alternate-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=339880#post339880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Beast case, what can be interpreted as &quot;feral&quot;? one must remember their seeming reflects the &quot;literary&quot;concept associated to animals rather than the real deal. Example: regal lions, cowardly hyenas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in a similar boat, here. It feels like acting in a feral manner (at least as I understand it) works well enough for Beasts tied to wild animals, but does less for those tied to domesticated ones. For my part, traits particular to an animal -- be they the &quot;real&quot; animal's physical nature or especially the anthropomorphized traits attributed to it -- are the ones I find most fun to play with, given the option. I just feel like the animal kingdom is broad enough that the Beast Blessing would benefit from depending on the character's animal, the way the Elemental Blessing depends on the character's element. I know Kiths sort of cover the &quot;specific animal&quot; side, but basically all of them are geared around the animal's physical nature. Pointing the Beast Blessing toward the symbolic/metaphorical side of the animal could be an option, maybe rewarding Beast characters for behaviors/approaches resonant with that side of their animals. Just... tricky to catch the spirit of that without making it too broadly applicable.<br /> <br /> I kinda don't want to make a fuss over it, but this is the one point in the rules hack that just didn't do anything for me. Which is a roundabout way of saying, &quot;Kudos on it as a whole!&quot; ^_^ I like the new Blessings that the Fairest and Wizened got, and the approach you've got toward Kiths also sounds like a good 'un.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T15:50:33-08:00","id":340263,"title":"","content":"OK, so I tweaked the Beast Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:58:49-08:00","id":341293,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'm musing on a different route for Kiths; I looked at what I worked on, and it felt too... compartmentalized. So I decided to experiment with a system of custom Kiths. <hr /><br /> Every Changeling suffered through their Durance differently; as much as a Keeper may attempt uniformity, their &quot;wards&quot; always end up diverging in some key point or another. Regardless, they all changed and were changed through-out their long stay in Faerie; their monstrous or magnificent Miens are a testament to that change.<br /> <br /> Each Changeling develops changes within their Mien; these changes are usually lumped together with similar changes in groups referred to as Kiths, thematically linked collections within a greater Seeming.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> After selecting their Seeming, a player should answer the following two questions:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Why was [Character's Name] stolen away?<br /> \u2022 How did the Durance change them?<br /> <br /> Using their Seeming and those questions as a guide, the player and their ST should sit down and go through the following steps together.<br /> <br /> <b>1 - Describe The Character</b><br /> <br /> The player should describes how they envision their character's Mien. Are they a mountain of animate snow? A rakish man with a smile that's FAR too wide? An old hag whose hair is liquid sunlight? If they are having difficulty, the ST should certainly toss in suggestions. It's important to keep in mind that the Strangers lack imagination; it is perfectly OK to describe a character's Mien in terms of a favorite fictional character.<br /> <br /> <b>2 - Decide on a Mechanical Bonus</b><br /> <br /> After deciding on the character's Mien, the player should select one of the options off the following list.<br /> \u2022 The character gains a +3 bonus on rolls within [circumstance].<br /> \u2022 The character adds +2 to a Resistance Trait (or applies a -2 penalty to another character's roll) within [circumstance].<br /> \u2022 The character adds +2 to a derived trait within [circumstance].<br /> \u2022 The character adds or subtracts 2 from their Size or an Attribute for the purposes of [circumstance].<br /> \u2022 The character has a +0L Brawl weapon built into their Mien.<br /> \u2022 The character may conjure a specific Size 1 melee weapon in [circumstance]; it decays into moondust and dreams moments after it leaves the Changeling's hands.<br /> \u2022 The character has Armor 1/1 built into their Mien.<br /> \u2022 The character may inflict a specific, minor Personal Tilt on another character with an appropriate roll.<br /> \u2022 The character may, when harvesting Glamour from Emotions in a way that involves physical contact, transfer a point of Willpower or a HL full of Bashing or Lethal damage to or from their target.<br /> <br /> The circumstances in which the bonuses occur must be narrower than the circumstances where they can get a bonus from their Seeming. While there can certainly be overlap, they should not always coincide.<br /> <br /> <b>3 - Rounding Everything Off</b><br /> <br /> After deciding on the hard mechanical bonus of the Kith, the player and the ST should come up with a &quot;narrative convenience&quot;, a minor power that should emphasize what the character was taken for. Whether its a Fairest whose voice carries further than it should, an Elemental who can talk to the rain, or a Beast who can breath underwater like the fish they were (and are), it should be some small but flavorful addition to the character, representing an inhuman feature of their Mien.<br /> <br /> <b>4 - Wrapping it Up</b><br /> The player and the ST should then work on a quick one or two sentence write-up of the exact benefits the player's Kith gives them, giving the powers a thematic name. The ST should take note of it; they may want to use it for an NPC at some later point.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional - Pre-Built Kiths</b><br /> <br /> An ST might desire a little extra control on the process of selecting a Kith, or could simply wish to push a theme. In that case, the ST should predesign a few Kiths, skipping over step 1. Then a player just needs to pick a Kith and describe their character. If their group had previously constructed a Kith, the ST should feel free to hold on to it and offer it as a pre-built Kith.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory - The Boundaries of Kiths</b><br /> <br /> Kiths are ultimately subsets of a greater Seeming, and therefore should be related to the overarching theme of the Seeming. Beasts should be ultimately be animals, for example, while Darklings should somehow tie back into the sheltering darkness. <hr /><br /> <b>Examples:</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 Ted is a player in Rita's Changeling game, and he wants to play a Beast based on an Owl. When he describes, his character, he emphasizes the wide, unblinking eyes and the strange silence of his feathered body.<br /> Mechanically, he chooses to give Mr. Hoots (Ted's terrible at names) the following Kith:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Nightstalker</b><br /> These Beasts were predators in the night, hunting down their prey in terrible silence. They are still a <b>Silent Killer</b>; they impose a -2 penalty on all Perception rolls made to locate them based off of hearing. In addition, as long as there is at least starlight, they can see as if it were bright as day.</div>Rita could then hold onto the Nightstalker Kith and offer it to players in future games.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Beth is another player in Rita's game, and has decided to play a Fairest; moreover, she's decided that her character was taken to Faerie because of her radiant smile. After some deliberation, Beth and Rita come up with the following:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Shinesmile</b><br /> These Fairest often look fairly ordinary until they crack a bright, toothy grin. They can always show of <b>Those Pearly Whites</b>, a smile so bright it can strike someone blind. By rolling Presence + Expression - 3, they may give someone the Blind tilt in both eyes until the beginning of their next turn. Their teeth are also always immaculately white, and they never develop cavities or need a crown.</div><hr /><br /> I'm pretty happy with the versatility here; a group should build up a repertoire of interesting Kiths over a few games, or could even have a brainstorming session before a chronicle where they make up a few Kiths.<br /> <br /> I wait with baited breath for someone to yell at me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-16-2014, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T22:14:00-08:00","id":341584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wait with baited breath for someone to yell at me. </div> </div> </div>Why would I yell at you? This system for kiths is great. One thing that I felt a little unsure about asking is this: why does Touch of Glamour only cost 1 glamour? It does scale with Wyrd AND lasts for the remainder of the scene. That's very powerful. It also makes some Contract clauses obsolete, such the first and third clauses of Stone. What do you plan on doing about that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-16-2014, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T22:22:39-08:00","id":341588,"title":"","content":"And <b>Mantles!</b><br /> <hr /><br /> Being a member of a Court grants access to certain perks; beyond the normal &quot;not being found by the Gentry&quot; benefit, courtiers also gain one additional point of Glamour whenever they harvest Glamour from a particular emotion, dependent on the Court in question.<br /> <br /> However, certain true perks are hidden behind a Court's Mantle, a metaphysical cloak that a Changeling can draw around themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Membership in a Court<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Characters may add their Mantle dots to Social rolls they make with regards to other characters that are a member of the Court. In addition, they gain a special benefits as their number of dots in this merit increase:<br /> <b>[1]:</b> The character's Mien begins to shift slightly, showing their adoption of their Court's Mantle; they may learn their Court's Contracts as Affinity contracts, and gain their Court's Minor Boon.<br /> <b>[3]:</b> At this point, the character is recognizably a member of their Court; they gain the benefits of their Court's Kith in addition to their original Kith, though they get to choose their &quot;narrative convenience&quot;.<br /> <b>[5]:</b> The character is the pinnacle of the Court's representation; they are eligible to be Crowned, and gain their Court's Major Boon.<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Spring Court</b></span><br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Desire.<br /> <b>Court Contracts:</b> Eternal Spring, Fleeting Spring<br /> <b>Minor Boon:</b> The Courtier gains a dot of Striking Looks related to beauty or desirability; this can allow them to have Striking Looks \u2022\u2022\u2022.<br /> <b>Major Boon:</b> The Courtier always starts off with a Good Impression when using Social Maneuvering on someone that they haven't met before.<br /> <b>Court Kith - Bloomchildren:</b> This Kith belongs to the Spring Court, and is inevitably developed by those that delve deeply into its secrets. Universally lively and enticingly &quot;innocent&quot;, Bloomchildren benefit from brief <b>Spring Flings</b>; the character gains a +3 bonus on any roll to entice or seduce a character they've known for less than a day.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Summer Court</b></span><br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Wrath.<br /> <b>Court Contracts:</b> Eternal Summer, Fleeting Summer<br /> <b>Minor Boon:</b> Whenever the Courtier spends Willpower to add dice to a Strength roll, they add 5 dice instead of 3.<br /> <b>Major Boon:</b> The Courtier is immune to the Beaten Down condition, and have an additional Health Level.<br /> <b>Court Kith - Summerbloods:</b> These Changelings are filled with anger and passion of Summer, driving them forward, motivated by <b>Purest Rage</b>; the character benefits from Armor 1/1 from the rage in their skin, turning aside blades and bullets alike. This armor stacks with any actual armor they may wear.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Autumn Court</b></span><br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Fear.<br /> <b>Court Contracts:</b> Eternal Autumn, Fleeting Autumn<br /> <b>Minor Boon:</b> Whenever the Courtier uses <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?674984-Changeling-the-Lost-Wyrd-Sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Wyrd Sorcery</a>, they add a +2 bonus to their roll.<br /> <b>Major Boon:</b> An Autumn Courtier using Wyrd Sorcery ignores the first Twist on their spell.<br /> <b>Court Kith - Spookshows:</b> Autumn Courtiers are scary, and they know it; perhaps its their blank eyes, scaly grins, or jutting limbs? Whatever the case, it can't be denied that they take <b>Ghoulish Delight</b> in fear; the Courtier may give another Character the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144034-fan-made-conditions?p=145963#post145963\">Cowed Tilt</a> using social skills other than Intimidate.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Winter Court</b></span><br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Sorrow.<br /> <b>Court Contracts:</b> Eternal Winter, Fleeting Winter<br /> <b>Minor Boon:</b> Other characters who spend Willpower to enhance a roll resisted by the Courtier only gain one extra die instead of three.<br /> <b>Major Boon:</b> The Courtier may ignore the Extreme Cold tilt entirely.<br /> <b>Court Kith - Chillhearts:</b> These Changelings are filled with sorrow, both for time lost in their Durance and for those who haven't yet escaped. Their brows are heavy, and their eyes are always filled with tears, because they are <b>Drowning in Misery</b>; any Perception rolls to notice the Changeling made by characters that aren't specifically looking for them take a -2 penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T12:50:34-08:00","id":380392,"title":"","content":"Coming back to this (I lost a bit of steam from doing this after the stuff for Changeling 2e got released; I'm gonna be obsolete :cry), I've come up with some different thoughts (and would like to hear about the Mantles.)<br /> <br /> <i>First off</i>, I never pasted the Mechanicals into this thread. Here they are (original concept by ??? (Please tell me if you know.)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Touch of Glamour:</b> Mechanicals may use the Touch of Glamour to enhance Crafts, Computers, and Intelligence rolls.<br /> <b>Blessing:</b> All Mechanicals receive a free speciality, and receive the 8-again property on all rolls within that Speciality.<br /> <b>Curse:</b> Mechanicals are incredibly specialized; they take a -1 penalty any rolls made with Untrained skills. In addition, they lose the 10-again quality on all non-Perception Wits rolls.</div><i>Second of all</i>, I've been thinking about Touch of Glamour and what it was supposed to do; I initially did it in comparison to the whole Blood Buffing things that Vampires do. Looking back, I'm not sure that was a good idea; therefore, I'm considering the following:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Touch of Glamour:</b> A Changeling may bring a brief touch of the Glamour dripping from their form to bear against a problem; they may spend Glamour to enhance dice pools and resistance traits that involve the Attributes or Skills listed for their Seeming. While this does not count towards the number of times they can spend Willpower in a turn, they may only spend Glamour to enhance a given action or resistance once. They may still spend Willpower on the roll or resistance trait as normal.</div>Does that look too strong or too weak to anyone? It <i>would</i> apply to Contract activation rolls, because <i>reasons</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Third of all</i>, if I organized this into a PDF or webpage, would anyone want a copy? It would be quick; an intro, two pages for Seemings, a page on building Kiths, and rules for Wyrd Evolution (Which I haven't posted to this thread yet. I should get on that.)<br /> <br /> Responses are desired!<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Here's an alternate Blessing for the Mechanicals, which is more in line with the other Seemings:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Blessing:</b> All Mechanicals gain a +2 bonus on any action taken while following someone else's instructions to the letter.</div> <br /> Because machines don't improvise.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 01-25-2015, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T17:49:19-08:00","id":381462,"title":"","content":"As an alternative for the Fairest blessing, what about a +2 bonus when the Fairest is &quot;in their comfort zone&quot; or &quot;engaging in an activity befitting his or her Kith.&quot; To me that gets more to the root of Fairest mindset. When you are in control you have exceptional control, which *enables* you to take the spotlight. But when you lose control, you lose big. Not every Fairest tries to be in the spotlight just for the sake of it. With this blessing, just like the True Fae, the Fairest is &quot;more than&quot; others who share their Kith. They epitomize, they *are*. Having the spotlight is an after-effect rather than the source of power, to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T17:58:29-08:00","id":381466,"title":"","content":"Hmm... that actually sounds like a better fit than what I've got; &quot;befitting their Kith&quot; is not a good one, since that means that Kith and Seeming bonuses will <i>always</i> overlap. But &quot;while in control&quot; is a better one.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on the Mantles or on the Kith building system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T18:20:31-08:00","id":381483,"title":"","content":"On Mantle:<br /> <br /> 1) I'm not sure I like Mantle 5 being a requirement for being crowned. I like the idea of &quot;sword in the stone&quot; King Arthur tales, where the unlikely nobody takes the crown. I think if you restrict it to Mantle 5 you lose something important and don't gain much. But, tell me why I'm wrong. X)<br /> <br /> 2) On the blessings from Mantle, it seems like the courts inconsistently give blessings related to the physical expression of the season and the emotional expression of the season. Spring blessings don't really have anything to do with desire or spring, but instead are social bonuses--I'd love to see Spring's blessings be more related to the season instead of being &quot;extra fairest stuff.&quot; Summer's buffs are all about wrath/combat, but nothing to do with the season of summer. Autumn's buffs are about using magic better, but have nothing to do with fear or the season. Winter, to me, has the best balance. The minor blessing impacts opponents with the sorrow emotion, limiting how much they can resist the Winter's power. The major blessing is directly related to the *season*.<br /> <br /> I would like to see this sort of dichotomy with each season. One blessing which is rooted in the court emotion, one blessing which is rooted in the season itself. I'm going to try to work up some examples, but do you see what I mean generally?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: example added<br /> <br /> Not sure on the power level of these, but brainstorm ideas for theme. The minor boon is intended to express the blooming of life in spring, while the major boon is intended to represent your mastery of the court emotion. Alternatively, you might have a minor boon expressing the emotion and a major boon expressing the season (as with Winter).<br /> <br /> Spring:<br /> Minor Boon: The font of life blooms from you. Once per scene, if you suffer damage which would result in a killing blow, you instead immediately fall unconscious one damage short of death. This does not end ongoing damage effects, but may stave off death from such effects for a turn.<br /> Major Boon: You have a natural understanding of the desires of those around you. After five minutes of social interaction with an individual, you may spend a Willpower point to identify their Virtue and Vice. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","user":"mjspra2","date":". 01-25-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T18:50:00-08:00","id":381494,"title":"","content":"On the Court Kith: I don't really like this concept. If these kiths are court-exclusive, it seems to become problematic if someone changes courts. Even if they're open to everyone but just given a special bonus for fitting the court, I would be concerned about seeing too many people taking the same kith.<br /> <br /> Part of what's awesome about Changeling is the variety of character concepts. If you have a single kith which is your court's specialty, lots of people will want to take it and we'll have less variety. I would nix this part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T19:10:35-08:00","id":381508,"title":"","content":"1) That was the way it was with the original; the idea being that people with more Mantle where more &quot;iconic&quot; of the Court. It also depends on if I hack the Crown; if I hack it so it isn't cray-cray, maybe I'll lower that requirement.<br /> <br /> 2) The funny thing is that I was attempting to translate the original blessings, and Winter's blessings came about because the original one was &quot;you are really good at <i>not being a part of the scene at hand.</i>&quot; Seriously, wot m8?<br /> <br /> But if you want them all to be based off of how I handled Winter...<br /> <br /> <b>Spring<br /> Minor:</b> Spring Courtiers are excellent at making people <i>want</i> to give them Glamour; whenever the Courtier harvests Glamour from another character's Desire, they may spend one Willpower to cause that character to regain one Willpower. This has the same rush as satisfying a Vice.<br /> <b>Major:</b> Any action that encourages growth or a new beginning performed by the Courtier receives a +2 bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>Summer</b><br /> <b>Minor:</b> Summer Courtiers are forever ready to bring violence upon their enemies; Summer Courtiers cannot be prevented from spending Willpower to enhance attacks, and do not have to spend Willpower to attack characters that have surrendered. When a Summer Courtier spends Willpower to enhance an attempt to hurt someone, they receive 4 dice instead of 3.<br /> <b>Major:</b> The Courtier may ignore the Extreme Heat tilt entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn</b><br /> (is a bit difficult; they were always the &quot;magic&quot; court. But I'll give it a go.)<br /> <b>Minor:</b> Whenever the Courtier harvests Glamour from fear caused by Supernatural means, they receive two additional glamour instead of just one.<br /> <b>Major:</b> Other characters within a Scene that contains the Courtier only receives two dice if they spend Willpower to restart something, but receive four dice if they spend Willpower on an attempt to bring a project to a conclusion.<br /> <br /> <i>That Autumn Major was a JERK and I hate it. Basically, the idea is that Autumn is the season of Endings; it's the time of year where you are supposed to be bringing everything to a conclusion. Spring Major is equally good at making new friends and growing flowers, and Summer Minor is because RAGE!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T19:40:40-08:00","id":381537,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick response! These are all good at matching the seasons. There's plenty of time to adjust them to get the &quot;just right&quot; abilities so I wont delve into mechanical balance but on theme. For the major boons, I would like to see courtiers gain something new. A new mechanic, a new option, a clear edge. For Summer and Winter, ignoring Extreme Heat / Cold might open up doors which are otherwise unavailable--depending on whether or not these abilities can be duplicated with contracts. Autumn is a little better--you can harvest with far greater potency than others, which could allow the Autumn courtier a big advantage in resupplying their resources--and that keeps with the other Autumn theme of being the magicians hehe. For Spring, you're only getting a +2 bonus which isn't really that interesting. I would probably change this one to be less general-purpose and more advantageous when it comes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}